"""Public installation guide. No secrets are accepted by this page."""
HTML = '''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Connect AC Papers</title><style>
:root{font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;color:#20342e;background:#f6f5f0}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0}main{max-width:960px;margin:auto;padding:52px 30px 72px}a{color:#255d46;text-underline-offset:4px}header{border-bottom:2px solid #294c3b;padding-bottom:28px;margin-bottom:30px}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:2px;font-weight:700}h1{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:clamp(38px,6vw,62px);font-weight:400;letter-spacing:-2px;margin:18px 0}header p{max-width:650px;line-height:1.65;color:#57665e}.step{display:grid;grid-template-columns:55px 1fr;gap:18px;padding:26px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #d3dbd1}.num{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:32px;color:#78917d}h2{margin:3px 0 12px;font-size:21px;font-weight:600}p,li{line-height:1.65}p{margin:10px 0}button,.button{display:inline-block;border:1px solid #28523d;background:#28523d;color:white;padding:11px 18px;border-radius:4px;font:inherit;cursor:pointer;text-decoration:none;margin:4px 8px 4px 0}.secondary{background:transparent;color:#28523d}code{font-size:13px;overflow-wrap:anywhere;background:#e6ebe2;padding:3px 5px}pre{background:#e6ebe2;padding:16px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.7;border-left:3px solid #9cae96}.hint{font-size:13px;color:#5f6e63}.flow{font-size:14px;border-top:1px solid #bccaba;padding-top:20px;margin-top:30px;line-height:1.8}.tag{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1px;border:1px solid #acbda5;padding:6px 8px;display:inline-block}details{margin-top:22px}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}.checks{padding-left:20px}footer{margin-top:32px;font-size:13px;color:#607163}@media(max-width:600px){main{padding:28px 20px}.step{grid-template-columns:30px 1fr;gap:12px}.num{font-size:26px}h1{letter-spacing:-1px}button,.button{font-size:14px}}
</style><main><header><div class="eyebrow">ACCELERATION CONSORTIUM · PUBLICATION WATCH</div><h1>Connect AC Papers.</h1><p>A quiet weekly digest in your private conversation. New publications are checked daily, saved to the paper system, and collected into a thread with links and feedback buttons.</p><span class="tag">82 AUTHORS IN THE INITIAL WATCHLIST</span></header>
<section class="step"><div class="num">01</div><div><h2>Create your Slack App</h2><p>Open Slack Apps, choose <b>Create New App → From a manifest</b>, select your workspace, and paste the configuration below. Then select <b>Install to Workspace</b> under OAuth &amp; Permissions.</p><button id="copy">Copy app configuration</button><a class="button secondary" href="https://api.slack.com/apps" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Slack Apps ↗</a><a href="/manifest.json" download="slack-manifest.json">Download JSON</a><p class="hint" id="copied" aria-live="polite">Permissions: send messages, open your direct conversation, and handle /papers commands. The app does not request access to channel history.</p></div></section>
<section class="step"><div class="num">02</div><div><h2>Save credentials securely</h2><p>On your computer, open a terminal in <code>tools/author-paper-monitor</code> and run:</p><pre>../../backend/.venv/bin/python deploy/connect_slack.py</pre><p>The installer asks for the <b>Bot User OAuth Token</b> from OAuth &amp; Permissions and the <b>Signing Secret</b> from Basic Information. Paste them into the hidden terminal prompts. They are stored encrypted in AWS.</p><p class="hint">Do not paste credentials into chat or this webpage. The installer verifies the workspace and gives you a connection code valid for one hour.</p></div></section>
<section class="step"><div class="num">03</div><div><h2>Preview privately, then start</h2><p>In Slack, run these commands. AC Papers will open a private conversation with you; no group channel receives messages:</p><pre>/papers connect YOUR_CONNECTION_CODE
/papers test
/papers start</pre><p><b>Wait for the preview before running start.</b> You should see one private test summary and up to three real-paper cards in its thread. Try a feedback button, then visit the app’s Home tab.</p><p class="hint">The person who enters the connection code becomes the operator. Only this person can change the author list or delivery settings.</p></div></section>
<details><summary>What happens after connection?</summary><ul class="checks"><li>Daily collection: 12:17 UTC. Weekly digest: Mondays at 12:17 UTC.</li><li>The first collection establishes a historical baseline; older papers are not announced as new.</li><li>81 author identities have been selected. Alan Veerman is retained for identity review; an ORCID or representative publication is needed to activate him.</li><li><code>/papers authors</code> opens the watchlist. <code>/papers add</code> lets you review candidate author profiles before adding one.</li><li><code>/papers pause</code> stops Slack updates while collection continues. <code>/papers status</code> shows the last successful run.</li><li>Feedback is saved for review; it does not automatically delete or hide papers.</li></ul></details>
<details><summary>Recommended: use a free OpenAlex API key</summary><p>Anonymous requests share a daily network quota. Get your own free key using <a href="https://help.openalex.org/api/authentication/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenAlex’s instructions</a>, then run:</p><pre>../../backend/.venv/bin/python deploy/configure_openalex.py</pre><p class="hint">This is independent of Slack installation. The next collector run and author search use the encrypted key automatically.</p></details>
<details><summary>Troubleshooting</summary><p><b>No preview:</b> verify the App’s token and signing secret, then check <code>/papers status</code>. Installation may require your workspace administrator’s approval.</p><p><b>Expired connection code:</b> run <code>deploy/connect_slack.py --new-code</code> with the same Python command. Reconnecting pauses updates until the private conversation passes its preview.</p><p><b>Cannot create an app:</b> ask a workspace administrator to install it from the supplied manifest. No local machine needs to stay running.</p></details>
<div class="flow">AUTHOR IDENTITIES → OPENALEX → DUPLICATE CHECK → PAPER SYSTEM → WEEKLY SLACK THREAD</div><footer>Indexing delays and author-profile errors can occur. Use the card’s report action to flag an incorrect match. This service does not scrape Google Scholar.</footer></main>
<script>document.getElementById('copy').onclick=async()=>{try{const r=await fetch('/manifest.json');if(!r.ok)throw Error();const v=await r.json();await navigator.clipboard.writeText(JSON.stringify(v,null,2));document.getElementById('copied').textContent='Copied. Paste into the JSON tab in Slack’s app manifest form.'}catch(e){document.getElementById('copied').textContent='Use Download JSON, then copy the file contents into Slack.'}};</script></html>'''
